cff-version: 1.2.0
title: CuraFrame
message: >
  If you use CuraFrame in academic, technical, or policy-related work,
  please cite it using the information below.
type: software

authors:
  - given-names: Don Michael
    family-names: Feeney Jr.
    email: dfeen87@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent Researcher

abstract: >
  CuraFrame is a constraint-driven framework for transparent, safety-first
  reasoning about hypothetical therapeutic designs. It evaluates explicit
  pharmacological and population-specific limits, causing unsafe ideas to fail
  early, clearly, and audibly—without automating discovery. CuraFrame is designed
  to support rigorous reasoning, documentation, and auditability rather than
  autonomous drug design.

keywords:
  - therapeutic safety
  - constraint-based reasoning
  - pharmacology
  - hypothetical design
  - AI safety
  - bioethics
  - risk mitigation
  - transparent reasoning

